---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Knowledge Hub" description="Honeypot IDS System — an integrated knowledge hub with interactive demos">
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>🐝 Honeypot IDS Knowledge Hub</h1>
    <p>
      A high-interaction deception platform that <span class="hype">captures, scores, and isolates</span>
      attackers in real time. Explore the architecture, dive into the detection pipeline,
      run interactive simulations, and understand every function — all in one place.
    </p>
    <a href="/docs" class="btn">Explore Docs</a>
    <a href="/sim" class="btn secondary">Run Simulator</a>
    <a href="/demo" class="btn secondary">Live Demo</a>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);">
      <div class="stat"><div class="num">14+</div><div class="label">Seeded CVEs</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="num">70+</div><div class="label">Suricata SIDs</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="num">11</div><div class="label">Routing Stages</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="num">18</div><div class="label">Unit Test Files</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>🎯 What This System Does</h2>
      <p>
        A WordPress/WooCommerce storefront that looks and behaves like a real shop — but sits behind an
        OpenResty (Nginx + Lua) reverse proxy that scores every request in real time and transparently
        diverts suspicious sessions into isolated, full-fidelity honeypot clones. Legitimate customers
        never notice; attackers get a convincing, exploitable target while every move is recorded.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>🚀 Quick Navigation</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <a href="/docs/detection" class="card">
          <h3>🔍 Detection</h3>
          <p>Multi-layered detection pipeline: URI patterns, CVE matching, Suricata IDS, IP reputation, automation detection, sophistication classification, honeytokens.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/observability" class="card">
          <h3>📊 Observability</h3>
          <p>Vector → Elasticsearch → Kibana pipeline. 7 dashboards + pattern report timeline. Structured security events.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/operations" class="card">
          <h3>⚙️ Operations</h3>
          <p>Two-host and single-host deployment, production hardening, troubleshooting runbooks, pool management.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/testing" class="card">
          <h3>🧪 Testing</h3>
          <p>18 pure-Lua unit test files, dashboard validation, blind pentest evaluation protocol.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/architecture" class="card">
          <h3>🏗️ Architecture</h3>
          <p>Request pipeline, two-host split, Lua module architecture, pooling system.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/reference" class="card">
          <h3>📖 Reference</h3>
          <p>Glossary, known issues, roadmap, changelog, literature, complete function reference.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/sim" class="card">
          <h3>🎮 Simulator</h3>
          <p>Interactive request scoring simulator. See how the detection pipeline scores real requests.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/demo" class="card">
          <h3>🔬 Live Demo</h3>
          <p>Live honeypot demonstration with real-time detection visualization.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>🏗️ Architecture Overview</h2>
      <div class="demo-box">
        <h3>Request Pipeline</h3>
        <pre><code>Client Request → Nginx access_by_lua_block → pattern_analyzer.analyze_request()
  → router.decide_route() (11 stages) → pool_router.get_or_assign_pool()
  → session_handler.update_session() → Redis session_store
  → Suricata eve.json → init_worker.lua → threat_intel shared dict
  → abuseipdb_client.report_ip_async() → AbuseIPDB</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>📋 Honest Assessment</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>✅ Strengths</h3>
          <ul style="color: var(--muted); padding-left: 1.2rem;">
            <li>Multi-layered detection (11+ stages)</li>
            <li>Explainable, auditable scoring</li>
            <li>Per-attacker isolation</li>
            <li>Elastic honeypot pools</li>
            <li>No tarpit (identical latency)</li>
            <li>Privacy-preserving GDPR identity</li>
            <li>Honeytoken injection</li>
            <li>18 unit test files</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>⚠️ Limitations</h3>
          <ul style="color: var(--muted); padding-left: 1.2rem;">
            <li>Same-host Suricata testing gap</li>
            <li>Decay system complexity (4 params)</li>
            <li>Honeytoken coverage (5 types)</li>
            <li>No ML (rule-based only)</li>
            <li>Redis single point of failure</li>
            <li>Pool scaling limits</li>
            <li>No end-to-end integration tests</li>
            <li>Dashboard drift risk</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>